    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1184">

                <pb facs="0971" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/1183c.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Secretary of the Treasury</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 18, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that this
                    Department has received definite information through its Consular Service that
                    Vera Cruz, Mexico, is now in the hands of insurrectionary forces.</p>
                <p>In view of the shipments of arms and munitions of war that are likely to be
                    excepted by the President for routing via Vera Cruz, or that have already been
                    so excepted, I have the honor to request that your Department take such action
                    as may be necessary to hold up all shipments which are to enter Mexican
                    territory through that port until this Department can satisfy itself that
                    conditions are such as to warrant forwarding such articles by the route referred
                    to.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
